{"metadata":{"slug":[{"Plain":"Arthur–Selberg迹公式"},0],"ext":[{"Plain":"md"},1],"tag":[{"Plain":"百科"},3],"title":[{"Plain":"“Arthur–Selberg 迹公式”"},2],"author":[{"Lazy":[{"Local":{"url":"SimplicialCat","text":"SimplicialCat"}}]},4]},"content":{"Lazy":[{"Plain":"\n<blockquote>\n<p>A key tool in the study of automorphic forms is the Arthur-Selberg trace formula, which expressed <strong>spectral quantities</strong> (traces on representations) in terms of <strong>geometric quantities</strong> (orbital integrals). — 恽之伟, Hitchin-type moduli spaces in automorphic representation theory</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>"},{"Local":{"url":"Hitchin模叠","text":"Hitchin 模叠"}},{"Plain":"</p>\n"}]}}